# Evidence, decisions, and governance records are not code surfaces.
# Raw research artifacts must never be reformatted (AGENTS.md §7);
# docs/ and decisions/ are prose records, not build inputs.
research/
docs/
decisions/
AGENTS.md
PLAYBOOK.md
CHECKLIST.md

# Migrated bodies are the source site's rendered HTML, carried verbatim so the
# reconciler can compare our page to the source's. A formatter rewriting them,
# however harmlessly, ends that. Same principle as `research/` above.
#
# EVERY entry body, not a list of directories. This used to name
# `content/blog/posts/` — a path from the project the kit was extracted from,
# which `content:transform` has never written to. `content/pages/` was
# protected and `content/posts/` was not, so on the first real migration
# `pnpm format` rewrote 642 migrated post bodies; measured, it removed a blank
# line from inside the source site's HTML. A custom post type writes to its
# own collection directory, so naming them one by one would have the same hole
# again the first time somebody configured one.
content/**/*.md
# …except the READMEs, which this repository writes and does format.
!content/**/README.md

